# Template drift allowlist for zudo-tauri-wisdom.
# Generated projects start from create-zudo-doc templates; this file lists
# intentional divergences from the pinned create-zudo-doc baseline so
# `pnpm check:template-drift` exits 0.
#
# Format: one repo-relative path per line (no leading slash).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# Reconciled against create-zudo-doc 5.16.1. Non-allowlisted scaffold files
# remain byte-identical to the pinned template; the five paths below diverge
# intentionally. The drift check scans templates/base plus the i18n feature.
#
# NOTE: `check_pair` in scripts/check-template-drift.sh returns on an allowlist
# hit BEFORE the file-existence check, so an allowlisted file that has gone
# stale against a newer baseline — or vanished — passes the gate silently. The
# five paths here must therefore be three-way compared (old template / new
# template / repo copy) by hand on every create-zudo-doc bump; a green
# check:template-drift says nothing about them.
#
# pages/index.tsx was listed until 4.4.13 and is deliberately NOT listed now:
# the wide home grid needed a hand-reconstructed route only while zudo-doc had
# no toggle for it (zudolab/zudo-doc#2959). 4.4.x ships `home.wide`, so the
# config carries the intent and the file is back to the locked 1-line re-export
# — one fewer host file to keep reconciled on every future bump.

# ── Host customization: brand + tight-token global.css ────────────────────
# global.css carries this site's font overrides (Noto Sans JP body + Futura
# display face) and the [data-header-logo] brand rule on top of the package's
# theme.css/content.css/features.css imports.
#
# 5.16.1: template unchanged since 5.13.1 — nothing upstream to adopt.
src/styles/global.css

# ── Generator patch: docHistory-wired doc-route stubs ─────────────────────
# The docHistory feature makes the generator patch both doc-route stubs to
# statically import DocHistory and merge it into createChrome's hostBindings
# (without the patch the doc-history button never hydrates on these routes).
# The patched stubs therefore diverge from the unpatched templates/base +
# features/i18n copies.
#
# NOTE (5.16.1): both stubs are byte-identical to the 5.13.1 templates plus that
# patch. 5.16.1 changed the templates in COMMENT PROSE ONLY — the header no
# longer claims the stub is REQUIRED because injected dynamic routes 404 in
# `zfb dev` (zfb serves them since 2.13.1); it now says the stub is retained for
# explicit host route ownership. Executable code is unchanged. Not adopted in
# the 5.16.1 sync (Takazudo/zudo-tauri-wisdom#76) because a concurrent task was
# building from these stubs; refresh the header prose on the next bump.
pages/docs/[[...slug]].tsx
pages/[locale]/docs/[[...slug]].tsx

# ── Host customization: doc-lookup skill generator ────────────────────────
# scripts/setup-doc-skill.sh is customized with this site's skill name
# (tauri-wisdom) and Claude + Codex targets, so it diverges from the template
# default. The skill it emits is gitignored.
#
# NOTE (5.16.1): upstream has moved further ahead of this fork, which predates
# all of it and still hard-codes `$REPO_ROOT/src/content/docs`, `docs-ja`, and
# `pnpm format:md`:
#   - nested-project / worktree correctness — PROJECT_PREFIX, REPO_DOCS_DIR,
#     MAIN_PROJECT_DIR and package.json-driven format-script detection
#     (zudolab/zudo-doc#2918), so the emitted SKILL.md points at the main
#     worktree's project dir instead of the current worktree;
#   - new in 5.14.0–5.16.1: the locale map is parsed out of zfb.config.ts
#     (defaultLocale / docsDir / locales) instead of probing for a docs-ja
#     directory, one symlink and one SKILL.md section per configured locale, and
#     an explicit warning against discovering roots with a `src/content/docs-*`
#     glob (it also matches version snapshots like `docs-v1-ja`).
# Deliberately NOT adopted here: porting it means re-forking a heavily
# customized file, which is a separate piece of work from a version bump.
# Recorded so it is not silently lost.
scripts/setup-doc-skill.sh

# ── Protocol-relative external links: check-links.js ──────────────────────
# The 5.13.1-era fork of this file (unquoted href/id parsing + entity decoding
# for zfb's minified production HTML) is GONE: zudolab/zudo-doc#3720 shipped
# that upstream, so this file is now the 5.16.1 template verbatim except for a
# single line. `//host/path` is an external protocol-relative URL, but the
# scaffold's scheme skip-list omits it, so it resolves as an internal path and
# is reported broken. One regex alternation restores that; covered by
# scripts/check-links.test.mjs. Not yet reported upstream.
scripts/check-links.js
